Modern LLMs are largely based on the Transformer architecture, which uses attention mechanisms to process contextual relationships between parts of the input.

LLMs can be used for:

Question answering
Text generation
Translation
Summarization
Sentiment analysis
Other NLP tasks

The key relationship is:   AI → Machine Learning → Deep Learning → Neural Networks → Transformers → LLMs

And the most important idea from this lesson is:
An LLM generates text by repeatedly predicting the next token based on the context, using learned parameters from large-scale training data.


================================================================Transformer================================================================
is a Deep learning architecture widely used for modern NLP/LLMs
A key mechanism in Transformers is Self-Attention. 
Self-Attention helps the model determine the relevance and relationships between words or tokens within the same sequence. 
This allows the model to build a better understanding of the context.

The original Transformer architecture contains two main components:
Encoder → Decoder

The Encoder processes the input text and converts it into numerical representations called vectors. These vectors capture contextual information about the input.
The Decoder uses these encoded representations to generate the output text.

